I've got an idea for a patch, and I just wanted to see if it's already
been done before I start mucking around in the code to implement it
myself.

A while back, my barbarian (Thvor; I'd started him before posting
here, so I just re-used the name...:-) found and tamed a little dog,
not expecting it to last long.  Then, he killed a chameleon, and the
dog quickly gobbled up the corpse.  Now, Thvor's got a pet Vampire
Lord.  Which is nice--he'll attack everything Thvor's fighting
against, and generally creams them.

Of course, the problem is that he'll also attack anything Thvor's
_not_ fighting.  Thvor went to a general store to price-I.D. some
stuff, and didn't think to close the door behind him; next thing he
knew, he'd inherited an entire store of junk, but still didn't know
the value of some of the stuff he was carrying.  Then, this morning,
he found an aligned temple (which, unfortunately, had multiple
entryways, not all of which could be closed...).  Thvor managed to buy
one level of protection before he had to start cleaning the blood off
of the altar.

So, anyhow, is there a patch to prevent pets from attacking peaceful
creatures (shopkeepers, priests, aligned unicorns, etc.)?  This seems
like a natural thing to want, especially for lawful/neutral
characters.  As it stands right now, Thvor can't even hit Vinny with a
rolled up newspaper...

If someone can point me to such a patch, that'd be great; failing
that, sections of code that are most likely to need fixing would be
very appreciated.  I'd also be interested in hearing any reasons why
pets should be allowed to attack peacefuls, just for completeness. 
:-)

